3. If the first integer is $3$, then one integer $p$ follows, meaning query the number at position $p$ $\bmod\ 998244353$.
4. If the first integer is $4$, then one integer $p$ follows, meaning undo the operation given on input line $p$ (guaranteed to be an addition or multiplication; no operation will be undone twice).

