Now there are $q$ queries. Each query gives three integers $x, y, l(0\leq x,y<n,1\leq l\leq n-max(x,y))$, asking: after the people from $x \sim x+l-1$ in the first row play against the people from $y \sim y+l-1$ in the second row, how many people in the first row will win.

